  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TFAQ eTrade for all coordination</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">eTrade for all is a multi-stakeholder initiative that aims to help developing countries better navigate the supply of technical assistance available from the international community, while at the same time providing donors with a clear picture of the relevant programmes offered by the various partners in their respective areas of expertise and mandate.
Over the past several years, UNCTAD has acquired a leadership role and a clear mandate in the area of e-commerce and the digital economy. UNCTAD provides coordinating functions for the initiative and is responsible for establishing and managing a dedicated online platform in three languages (English, French and Spanish), fostering synergies amongst partners according to their interests and mandates, and convening regular meetings, including through the UNCTAD eWeek.</narrative>
  </description>
